# MCP Selector Naming (Workspace)

## Invariant

- Use `tool` only for dispatch-style surfaces with `arguments: str = "{}"` and an internal subtool registry.
- Use semantic selector names like `op`, `method`, `operation`, or `action` when the tool exposes one stable shared schema with first-class typed arguments.
- Use no selector for single-purpose tools.

## Canonical Examples

- `dispatch(tool="validate_pipeline", arguments='{"pipeline": "rag-context"}')`
- `cortex(tool="entities", arguments='{"type": "person"}')`
- `agent_bus(tool="fetch", arguments='{"thread": "111"}')`
- `fs(sandbox="context", op="list", path="tasks/")`
- `fs(sandbox="workspaces", op="read", path="services/mcp-server/server.py")`
- `observability(operation="recent-failures", params={"limit": 20})`
- `manage(action="status")`

## Documentation Rule

- When updating MCP docs, examples must match the live selector shape in code.
- Do not describe dispatch surfaces as `op=` tools after migration.
